<title>SOUTH KOREA: Base issue prices for six S.Korean IPOs revised up.</title>
<headline>Base issue prices for six S.Korean IPOs revised up.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Securities Supervisory Board said on Tuesday the base issue prices for six of South Korea's seven initial public offerings due on July 23-24 had been revised upward as a result of sales to institutional investors.</p>
<p>Underwriters were authorised to sell 20 percent of the total amount of shares being offered, either through book-building or open auctions, a board official said.</p>
<p>Book-building refers to a procedure whereby institutional investors are asked to indicate the amount of shares they want and the price they are willing to pay.</p>
<p>Revised details on the seven IPOs are as follows:</p>
<p> COMPANY			  SHRS	PRICE (WON)     LEAD MGR</p>
<p>				  (000's)  REVISED  ORIGINAL</p>
<p> Yukong Gas Co		2,402     17,000    15,500  Samsung</p>
<p> Daou Technology Inc	  480     52,000    48,000  Boram</p>
<p> LG-Caltex Gas Co Ltd     2,060     18,500    16,500  Seoul</p>
<p> Yoo Sung Metal Co Ltd	273     13,000    11,000  Daewoo</p>
<p> Pantech Co Ltd		 440     65,000    60,000 Ssangyong</p>
<p> Younbo Chemical Co Ltd     290.4   36,000    31,000  Samsung</p>
<p> Poong Sung Electric Co Ltd 860    unchanged  19,000  Tongyang</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
